Source: vector-db-benchmark
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Redis Ltd. <oss@redislabs.com>
# cargo and rustc are NOT listed: the distros' own are too old for this crate
# and its lock file. scripts/release/build-deb.sh installs a current stable
# toolchain with rustup before calling dpkg-buildpackage, and checks it is on
# PATH. cmake and perl build the statically linked HDF5 / zlib / OpenSSL
# (--features release-static), so the package needs none of those libraries
# at run time, on any codename.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 12), cmake, perl, pkg-config, ca-certificates, git
Standards-Version: 4.4.1
Homepage: https://github.com/redis/vector-db-benchmark
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/redis/vector-db-benchmark
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/redis/vector-db-benchmark.git
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: vector-db-benchmark
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Framework for benchmarking vector search engines
 vector-db-benchmark runs upload and search workloads against vector
 databases (Redis Query Engine and Vector Sets, Valkey, Dragonfly, KiviDB,
 Qdrant, Elasticsearch, OpenSearch, pgvector, MongoDB, Turbopuffer, and
 more), with filtered, hybrid, sparse and full-text variants, and writes
 per-run JSON results with recall, throughput and latency percentiles.
 .
 The package installs the CLI (vector-db-benchmark), the dataset tools
 (prepare-msmarco, generate-dataset) and the reader micro-benchmarks
 (bench_npy, bench_jsonl, bench_hdf5 under /usr/lib/vector-db-benchmark).
 The dataset catalogue and the engine configurations the CLI reads from
 its working directory are installed under /usr/share/vector-db-benchmark.
 .
 HDF5, zlib and OpenSSL are linked statically; the binaries need only glibc.
